tlas/kansas/marshall-county"],["ARC or PLC in Marshall County","/arc-plc/kansas/marshall-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Marshall County record runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years. In 2025, February to March came in at 32% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, April to May sits at 133% of normal there. Grid 23836 had its driest year in 1988 at 52% of normal.</p>"}
